Allow VLNV-shaped names in `requires:` to bypass the name prefix.

compile-to-core unconditionally prepends `name_pfx` (default
`caliptra:compile_yml`) to every entry in a compile.yml `requires:`
list, with no escape hatch (pre_exec/post_exec/options/global are all
stripped). That means compile.yml-side consumers cannot declare a
dependency on a hand-written FuseSoC core (e.g.
`lowrisc:dv:dv_base_reg`), which is needed when generated cores must
anchor compile order against natively-owned library files.

Pass through any name that already contains a `:` -- treat it as a
fully-qualified VLNV and emit it verbatim. Bare names still get the
prefix as before.

--- a/src/compile_to_core/core.py
+++ b/src/compile_to_core/core.py
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@
                 as P:N.

     """
-    return [f"{name_pfx}:{r}" for r in requires]
+    return [r if ":" in r else f"{name_pfx}:{r}" for r in requires]


